2.3 Problem Definition
Given a task(I,𝑞)and a large language model L, our objective is
to rerank the elements in Iwith respect to the query 𝑞to minimize
the expected error, denoted as E(𝜀L(I,𝑞)). Specifically, from the
set of all possible rankings Π, we seek to identify the reranking
function𝜋∗:{1,2,...,𝑛} → { 1,2,...,𝑛}that rearranges each
element𝑒𝜋∗(𝑖)to a new position 𝑖in such a way that the response
of the LLM exhibits an improvement in terms of reduced expected
error.
